        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            A pickleball paddle lasts as long as it keeps playing the way you need it to. For casual players that can mean several years; for competitive players, often well under two. The face texture usually fades first, followed by core softening and dead spots, and none of it happens overnight, which is why comparing against a fresh paddle is the most reliable test.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Store your paddle out of the heat, protect the face, clean it gently and regrip it as needed, and it will usually wear out through play rather than damage. When it is time to replace it, use what the old one taught you about your game, and start with our best pickleball paddles roundup.
          </p>
